Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(kanban):=20operator=20call=20label=5Fpubli?=
 =?UTF-8?q?sh=20=E2=80=94=20hub-probed,=20one=20atomic=20Board=20labels=5F?=
 =?UTF-8?q?add=20[t=5F01a1cefefcad176a]?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

kanban_supervisor_request(ops=[{op:'operator', action:'label_publish', machine, labels, proof:{kind:'hub_probe'}}])
asks the hub to ADD skill:/capability: labels to one machine's Board registry entry.

- Executor: the hub (the gateway holding ~/.config/hermes-mail/admin.key). Workers never read the key or run an
  admin command; a non-hub gateway never takes a label_publish call, and a hub without the key refuses
  no_admin_key.
- Proof: the hub takes no claimed result. It re-runs its own probe of the machine
  (~/.local/share/hermes-worker-skills/bin/label-probe <machine>, the instance-role SSM read) and publishes a
  label only if that probe proves it (skill in the complete inventory, capability proof ok=true). One unproven
  label refuses the whole call bad_proof; an absent/failed probe fails it proof_unavailable.
- Labels: add-only delta, skill:/capability: only; machine:* and every other namespace refused (label_refused),
  re-validated on the hub.
- Write: ONE `hermes-mail admin machine <m> --add-labels` (Board labels_add, hermes-hub 3ddfe728a8 / client
  1.3.12). The Board applies the delta to the stored set inside its Durable Object transaction, so a concurrent
  writer's labels are never dropped and there is no client-side compare-and-set loop (three exact-head reviews
  found lost-write races in the earlier client CAS/repair loop; that loop is gone). A pre-read skips the write
  when every label is present (already_applied) and refuses unknown_machine / too_many_labels; the call is
  applied only when the Board's answer holds the whole delta, else failed.
- Result channel: operator_call_result on the requester's own card through the Board, accepted only when the
  Board vouches origin_gateway == hub (a self-written result is ignored).
- Probe + admin calls run in one background job thread (operator_label_jobs row; stale/dying jobs bounded,
  JOB_STALE_S 900 > worst 330 s; delivery backs off to ~12 h inside the 24 h deadline); every call logged in
  operator_calls (new target_machine column).
